278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (Before I even graduated high school, I knew I wanted to join Formula SAE. When I finally got to Concordia, I could not wait to meet the team and get started working on the car. Over my time on the team, I learned many different skills that are still valuable in my career as a design engineer. I learned hard skills such as manufacturing, simulation, design, and validation. But what was the most valuable to me were the soft skills I learned along the way. I was mentored by older members on the team, learning first how to be part of an operating team, then learning how to improve that team and later how to lead it. I also found great joy in passing the torch and mentoring younger students, and helping them improve as engineers. Joining this team was without a doubt the best decision I made during my time at Concordia. What I learned on this team through my time as Brakes and Suspension lead as well as team Captain is the main reason I was able to get to where I am today and why I can excel in my role as Mechanical Design Engineer. I am also extremely grateful to the supporters and sponsors whose generosity enables this team to exist, granting students the same opportunity that shaped my career.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
